@@ -3,3 +3,19 @@
 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` is exported from `src/index.ts` and resolves plain JSON Pointer
+strings as defined by [RFC 6901](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc6901.html):
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+resolvePointer({ users: [{ name: "Ada" }] }, "/users/0/name"); // "Ada"
+resolvePointer({ "a/b": true }, "/a~1b"); // true
+```
+
+The empty pointer returns the document itself. Tokens decode `~1` as `/` and `~0` as `~`.
+Invalid syntax, missing values, and invalid or out-of-range array indices throw an error.
+URI fragment strings such as `#/users/0` are not accepted. The document is not modified.
+
+Run the tests with `npm test` (Node.js 22.18 or newer, with TypeScript support enabled).
diff --git a/src/index.ts b/src/index.ts
